{
  "abstract": "Self-contained, pure-kernel Lean 4 formalization proving that for every integer n ≥ 3 (both odd and even), no unimodular Alltop phase function exists on 𝔽₂ⁿ and no n-qubit pure state generates 2ⁿ pairwise mutually unbiased orthonormal bases under the n-qubit Pauli (product Weyl–Heisenberg) group. Resolves Conjecture 1 and the unrestricted product-WH MUB question of Damski et al. (arXiv:2603.15550) and rules out the product WH-MUB maximizer mechanism conjectured by Liu, Low, and Yin (Quantum Sci. Technol. 11, 015035, 2026; Open Quantum Problem E28) for n ≥ 4. Also formalizes sharpness at n = 2, the strong odd-n two-valued Pauli-spectrum obstruction, the strict phase-state Gowers U³ bound > 2 - 2⁻ⁿ, and exact closed-form Pauli 4th moments for a GL(n, 𝔽₂)-invariant spike+uniform family recovering the 3-qubit Hoggar SIC (F₃ = 16/9) and certifying a 4-qubit unit state with F₄ < 2.150521. AI-assistance disclosure: the bulk of the technical work (proof discovery, Lean 4 formalization, companion scripts, and manuscript drafting) was carried out using AI systems under the author's problem selection, direction, and oversight; mathematical validity of all compared theorems rests on Lean 4's kernel verification.",
